WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.210
For decades, the central and eastern
United States averaged about 25 earthquakes

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.210
of magnitude 3 or more a year.

3
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.310
Then the count climbed.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.550
In 2015, the same region had 1,010.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:22.430
In Oklahoma alone, the yearly count
went from 41 in 2010 to 888 in 2015.

6
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.130
Had a new fault opened?

7
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.090
Was it just better instruments?

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.290
What changed?

9
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll read a seismogram,

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.370
using the gap between the P and S waves
to find how far away an earthquake struck.

11
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.670
You'll also compare
magnitude with intensity,

12
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.870
and see how strong shaking makes
saturated sediments lose their strength.

13
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.730
Your mission: find out what changed in
the central and eastern United States.
